#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Create six Matplotlib diagrams for Probe 305, 306, 308 or 309.

Place this file in sim_par_ink_prop/plots, then run (all four by default):
    python plot_probe305_306 --no-show
    python plot_probe305_306 --probe 308 --no-show
    python plot_probe305_306 --probe 309 --no-show
    python plot_probe305_306 --probe all --no-show

Dependencies: numpy, pandas, scipy, matplotlib; tzdata on Windows.
The selected measured window summaries and manual protocol values are embedded
below, so the original measurement CSV is not required. Optionally recalculate
the sensor summaries with --csv PATH. This does not change the manual weights
or dry-residue measurements. Times are local Europe/Berlin (MESZ).

The composition inversion preserves Pigment:PG:MG using the weighed recipe
(PG/pigment=2; MG/pigment is probe-specific). The first sensor point is anchored
to the known initial recipe. CONSTANT measurement-minus-model offsets are then
subtracted from every later measurement. Formal inverse solutions can violate
the evaporation-only assumption; these violations are reported, not removed.
Plot 6 independently inverts all selected points with the calibration field,
without anchoring P1 to the recipe or subtracting an additional sensor offset.
The resulting compositions are pointwise fits, not a validated evaporation path.

Temperature correction, separately for density and sound velocity:
    y_corrected = y_measured + h(composition, T_reference) - h(composition, T_i)
T_reference is the unweighted mean of selected point temperatures. Composition
is held at each point's InkCalculator inverse solution. The correction leaves
the constant offset in the measured signal and does not correct it twice.

Reference: GitHub niklasreeker/sim_par_ink_prop, commit b1c7bb792922992542dfbfe0f14c3e393bd15e65.
CSV: Messdaten_2026-10-03_12-42-45.csv; Notion protocol Probe 305.
Probe 306 source: Messdaten_2026-10-05_16-50-09.csv, commit
c33b3c0c08686de7545879c69ad87ec6c3e8f5fd; Notion protocol read 05 October 2026.
Probe 306: 60 m/min simulated, no printing, Impulsion 95%, Suction 100%, 80 C.
The protocol's second '11:35 MTU Stopp' is interpreted as 13:35, consistent
with the chronology and sensor transition; the source is not changed.
Sample masses are approximate, and tank jumps differ from those masses.
P4's sensor window is about 27-32 minutes after the sample/tank weighing.
No mass-loss rate is treated as an independently verified evaporation rate.
The P1 offset anchor is a conditional recipe assumption, despite pre-P1 loss.

Extension 15 October 2026: 308/309 use the Gaussian 9/10/11 field (saved
strength 0.70, bandwidth 0.30). The original IDW default remains for 305/306.
Use --calibration-field PATH to explicitly compare all probes with one field.
308/309 filter paired rho/c/T rows: SensOK=1, C_M>=1500, Rho_S<0.15,
C_S<1.5, C_Sp<5. Manual MA160/tank observations have their own timestamps.
MA160 308: bucket 2.08; 13:13 only 2.12/2.18. MA160 bucket 309 excluded.
309 S3/S4 follow pump changes and are labelled as diagnostic fits.
The recipe anchor is at S0; 309 S0 is the clean 11:54-11:59 window.
Repeated minutes before/after sampling are retained; no invented seconds.
New source CSV blob: 8125dce5f66619e4876224abc6deeebcbf1c82f3.
